NVCC 13.4 rejects GCC 16.2's mixed unqualified/ref-qualified substr overload
set. Keep the original ABI and substring results in CUDA host code by omitting
only the new rvalue storage-reuse overloads there. Ordinary C++ retains them.
The constructor implementations and the selected C++23 dialect stay intact.

--- a/bits/basic_string.h
+++ b/bits/basic_string.h
@@ -3469,7 +3469,7 @@
-#if __cplusplus >= 202302L
+#if __cplusplus >= 202302L && !defined(__CUDACC__)
       _GLIBCXX_NODISCARD
       constexpr basic_string
       substr(size_type __pos = 0) &&
       { return basic_string(std::move(*this), __pos); }
 
       _GLIBCXX_NODISCARD
